---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Snooze - Support"
  description="Get help with Snooze - Sleep Sounds, the iOS app."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/snooze/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Snooze?</p>
          <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Snooze%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I mix sounds?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">On the mixer, tap a sound to start it, then tap more to layer them, up to four. Snooze puts on a costume for the first sound in the mix. Each sound has its own volume slider; tap a sound again to take it out.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I set a sleep timer?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Tap the timer button at the top right of the mixer. Drag the star around Snooze&rsquo;s ring, or pick a length, choose how long the fade takes, then tap Start. In the last ten minutes Snooze gets sleepy, the sound fades out, and a few seconds later the screen goes dark too. Tap it to bring it back.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What is the morning check-in?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">The morning after a timer fades the sound out, Snooze asks how you slept. Tap a moon, from a sliver for a rough night to a full moon for a great one, and the night goes into your sleep log with the sounds you played. Tap Not now to skip it.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do presets and the widget work?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Build a mix and tap the save button next to Play to keep it as a preset. To put a preset on the Home Screen widget, touch and hold it in Presets and choose Show on the widget, then add Snooze from the widget gallery. The widget&rsquo;s button plays and pauses that preset without opening the app.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Will the sounds play all night?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. Without a sleep timer, the sounds keep playing with your screen locked or while you use other apps. Taking out your headphones pauses them, so they don&rsquo;t suddenly play from the speaker.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can music or a podcast play at the same time?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. In Settings, turn on Play alongside other apps. Snooze then plays under your other audio, but its controls can&rsquo;t appear on the Lock Screen or in Control Center.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I see the first-night walkthrough again?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. In Settings, tap Meet Snooze again.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does the app work offline?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. Every sound is made on your iPhone as it plays, so there&rsquo;s nothing to download and no internet connection is needed.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
